WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A short, practical one to close the MCP module: the three things that actually go wrong when you connect a server, and how to fix each one fast.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.636
One: the server won't start at all.

3
00:00:07.636 --> 00:00:10.766
Almost always the command is wrong, or the package didn't download.

4
00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:16.000
Run the exact command in a real terminal — you'll see the real error there, where it isn't swallowed by the app.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.581
Two: it connects, but lists no tools.

6
00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:20.701
Some servers only expose their tools after they've finished initializing.

7
00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:23.393
The fix is almost silly but it works: disconnect and reconnect.

8
00:00:23.393 --> 00:00:26.000
The second connection catches the tools the first one missed.

9
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.254
Three: authentication failures.

10
00:00:27.254 --> 00:00:31.217
For a stdio server, check the env token you set — a typo or an expired token is the usual culprit.

11
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:35.261
For an http server, just redo the OAuth sign-in; tokens expire, and re-authorizing gets a fresh one.

12
00:00:35.261 --> 00:00:37.000
Two different fixes for the two transports.

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.056
That's MCP end to end.

14
00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:42.328
Module 7 goes deep on tools themselves — every built-in group, and how to write your own.

15
00:00:42.328 --> 00:00:43.000
See you there.

